Infer a functional ``collections.namedtuple`` / ``typing.NamedTuple`` call without
crashing when a field name is an integer literal above the interpreter's integer
string conversion limit, such as ``namedtuple("T", [0xfff...])``. Mapping ``str()``
over the field names used to raise an uncaught ``ValueError``; such a value is not a
valid field name, so inference now yields ``Uninferable``.

Refs #3400
